invariant: INV-74
file: src/session.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh tcp_read
reason: tlsi_seal_alert returns CH_ECAP with whatever length rec_seal
  wrote when it refused the alert. record.h states no length for a
  refused record, and session.h states 0, so a ch_read_in_place that
  fails at the last sequence number could report a reply that holds no
  alert record. The real rec_seal writes none; the proof's stub writes
  any length and requires one alert record or nothing.

--- old
        *out_len = 0; // record.h states no length for a record it refused
        return CH_ECAP;
    }
    return CH_OK;
}
--- new
        return CH_ECAP;
    }
    return CH_OK;
}
